From 98deec15800b8b34bccb4d32474f1202b6543cbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 04:53:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] downport: clear the VALUE row work area between rows of
 different shapes

outlineValue builds every row of a table VALUE in one work area,
DATA tempN LIKE LINE OF ..., and never clears it, so a component a row
leaves out keeps what an earlier row put there instead of being initial:

  tab = VALUE #( ( name = 'A' qty = 5 ) ( name = 'B' ) ).

was downported to a second row with qty = 5. The same for an empty row
( ) after a filled one, under BASE, with an inline DATA( ) target, and
inside a LOOP/DO, where the FIRST row inherits the previous pass's last
row, as the generated DATA does not reinitialize anything.

Each row that is built in the work area now starts with
CLEAR tempN, followed by the shared prefix assignments
(VALUE #( sign = 'I' ( ... ) ( ... ) )), which are emitted at every row
instead of once before the first, so the prefix still applies to every
row. Rows that are a plain source, ( lv_line ), or LINES OF insert
directly and are unchanged.

The CLEAR is only emitted when a row can observe an earlier row: when
the rows assign different sets of components, or the prefix changes
between rows. Rows that all assign the same components, which covers
every FOR and the existing multi-row tests, downport exactly as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Kz1J78phfNKbqUaq3VcP4U
